2026-10-29T18:42Z haduong created

--- body ---
## Context

0004 names DOI downloads from Crossref metadata and warns on a title mismatch. ISBNs are left out
(`naming.py`: identifiers starting with `isbn:` are skipped), so a book is still named from `--title`,
or `Unknown_isbn:…` without one, and nothing checks the caller's title. ISBNs are not validated
either (DOIs are, by `validate_doi`): a mistyped ISBN goes straight to LibGen.

## Actions
1. Book metadata lookup in `naming.py`: Google Books `volumes?q=isbn:<isbn>` (title, authors,
   publishedDate in one call, no key), Open Library `/isbn/<isbn>.json` as fallback. Same name shape
   `<FirstAuthor> <Year> - <Title>`, same mismatch rule and `--keep-title`, same offline fallback.
2. ISBN-10/13 normalisation (strip hyphens and spaces) and check-digit validation, in `utils.py` next
   to `validate_doi`; an invalid ISBN is rejected before any fetch, like an invalid DOI.
3. Mock all network in tests.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] An ISBN fetched without a title gets an author-year-title name
- [ ] A title mismatch on an ISBN is logged and the file named from metadata, as for DOIs
- [ ] Invalid ISBN check digits are rejected with a clear error
- [ ] Tests cover all three; the suite passes
